# ==============================================================================
# qai-backend — Environment variable reference
# ==============================================================================
#
# This file is a CURATED template, not a complete dump of every env var the
# service reads. The authoritative list lives in the Zod schema at
# `src/config/environment/env.ts` — open that file to find every variable,
# its validation rule, and its default.
#
# What belongs here: env vars that DevOps needs to set or tune in production
# and that contain NO secrets. As new tunables ship, append a clearly-marked
# section below — don't silently rewrite existing sections, that creates
# merge conflicts during PR review.
#
# What does NOT belong here: secrets (DB password, API keys, Telegram tokens,
# etc.). Those live in the host's secret manager or `.env.local` (gitignored).
#
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Section: Phase 4 (May 2026) — Mobile regression concurrency tunables
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Copy the lines you want to override into your prod / staging / dev env.
# Values are read inside `concurrency-decision.ts` via a NaN-safe parser
# (Number.isFinite + >=1); garbage values fall back to the documented
# default rather than crashing the boot.
#
# IMPORTANT: do NOT raise REGRESSION_MOBILE_MAX_CONCURRENCY above 1 until
# Phase 3 (host-ADB mutex, branch `fix/host-adb-mutex` in qait-mobile-runner)
# is shipped to prod AND stress-tested for 7 days. Without it, parallel
# regressions race the daemon socket and surface `Client aborted` /
# `pm create-user failed`. See regression-run.service.ts:2079-2087 for the
# full pre-Phase-3 incident notes.
#
# Decision policy lives in
# `src/services/testing/regression/concurrency-decision.ts` —
# every env var here is an INPUT to that function, not a hard switch.
# Final cap is always min(MAX_CONCURRENCY, runnerPoolIdle, desiredCap).

# --- Hard ceiling (operator force-cap) ----------------------------------------
# Min 1. Sets the absolute maximum for ANY regression run regardless of pool
# state or test count. Default 1 preserves pre-Phase-4 serial behaviour, so
# this entry is a no-op until you explicitly bump it.
#
# Rollout suggestion:
#   - Week 1 (post Phase 3 deploy): keep at 1, verify Phase 4 log line
#     `[REGRESSION_RUN] Mobile concurrency decided` appears with cap=1
#   - Week 2: bump to 2, watch cold_start_count metric stay flat
#   - Week 3+: bump to 3 if pool size >= 3 and no race incidents
REGRESSION_MOBILE_MAX_CONCURRENCY=1

# --- Test-count split between small and large batches -------------------------
# testCount <= threshold → use SMALL_CAP. testCount > threshold → use LARGE_CAP.
# Default 5 means: 1-5 tests counted as small, 6+ as large. Tune up if you
# typically run larger regressions and want them to get the bigger cap.
REGRESSION_MOBILE_SMALL_BATCH_THRESHOLD=5

# --- Desired cap for small batches (testCount <= SMALL_BATCH_THRESHOLD) -------
# Subordinate to MAX_CONCURRENCY and runner poolIdle.
REGRESSION_MOBILE_SMALL_CAP=2

# --- Desired cap for large batches (testCount > SMALL_BATCH_THRESHOLD) --------
# Subordinate to MAX_CONCURRENCY and runner poolIdle. Usually equal to your
# runner's POOL_ANDROID_SIZE so a large regression saturates the pool.
REGRESSION_MOBILE_LARGE_CAP=3
SNAPSHOT_USE_CDP_PREVIEW=true
SNAPSHOT_USE_CDP_BACKGROUND=true

# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Section: Self-serve PLG signup (May 2026)
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Master switch for the B2C self-serve flow. Default false keeps the existing
# B2B behaviour (business-email gate + manual admin approval) fully intact.
#
# When true:
#   - new users are auto-approved on first auth (status='approved') and get a
#     default workspace + project, so they skip the onboarding wizard
#   - personal-email signups (Gmail etc.) are accepted; disposable still blocked
# The requireApproved middleware stays in place — flipping this off restores
# the gated flow with no code change. Implemented in
# `src/services/core/self-serve-provisioning.service.ts` +
# `src/services/auth/auth.service.ts`.
# Default false here so copying .env.example verbatim does NOT silently enable
# self-serve. Set to true per-deploy to turn on the B2C flow.
AUTO_APPROVE_SIGNUP=false